<BaseLayout
  title="Method v0.1"
  description="Audit the deterministic rules, evidence boundaries, privacy behavior, ownership disclosure and corrections process behind SEO Fan-out."
  canonicalPath="/methodik/"
  pageClass="reference-page"
>
  <header class="reference-hero">
    <p class="mono-label">Method v0.1 · August 2026</p>
    <h1>A planning model you can audit.</h1>
    <p>SEO Fan-out maps the work around a topic. It does not reveal private search-engine queries, model reasoning, rankings, demand, or citation probability.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="reference-section split-section">
    <div>
      <h2>What “fan-out” means here</h2>
      <p>Google publicly describes AI Mode using a query fan-out technique that issues related searches across subtopics and data sources. This tool borrows only the useful planning idea: one question usually has several evidence needs. Our branches are deterministic editorial prompts, not reconstructed platform activity.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="source-note">
      <strong>Primary public context</strong>
      <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/ai-mode-search/">Google: Introducing AI Mode, March 2025</a>
      <a href="https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/search/google-search-ai-mode-update/">Google: AI Mode updates, May 2025</a>
      <p>These sources define Google’s product description. They do not validate this site’s page decisions.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">The rule path</p>
      <h2>Four inputs. Five branches. One decision.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="method-flow" aria-label="Method steps">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>State the real question</h3><p>The topic is used verbatim. The tool does not infer demand or expand it into hidden keywords.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Choose the user job</h3><p>Learn, compare, choose, act, or troubleshoot. This changes the goal, questions, and source roles.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Declare coverage</h3><p>No page, partial coverage, substantial coverage, overlap, or an unknown inventory.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Declare evidence</h3><p>None, secondary-only, primary/firsthand, or observed/reproducible evidence.</p></article>
      <article><span>05</span><h3>Apply the conservative rule</h3><p>Existing ownership and weak evidence block new URLs before the tool ever recommends one.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="mono-label">Decision table</p>
      <h2>The exact v0.1 rule set</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Coverage</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Decision</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Several pages overlap</td><td>Any</td><td>Consolidate</td><td>Do not add to a competing set.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Partial existing page</td><td>Any</td><td>Strengthen</td><td>The user job already has a home.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Substantial page</td><td>Primary or observed</td><td>No action</td><td>Another URL adds little value.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Substantial page</td><td>None or secondary</td><td>Build evidence</td><td>Proof, not another page, is missing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No page</td><td>Primary or observed</td><td>Create one page</td><td>A distinct job and credible evidence exist.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No page</td><td>None or secondary</td><td>Build evidence</td><td>Do not publish ahead of proof.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Inventory unknown</td><td>Any</td><td>Build evidence</td><td>Inventory the site before choosing a URL.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section split-section" id="privacy">
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Privacy & retention</p>
      <h2>Your input stays in the page.</h2>
      <p>Version 0.1 is a static browser tool. It has no account, analytics, server endpoint, paid provider, database, cookie, or local-storage write. Copy and JSON export happen only after your direct browser action.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Uncertainty</p>
      <h2>Modeled means reviewable—not true by default.</h2>
      <p>The result is a structured prompt for editorial judgment. Check real URLs, current primary sources, rights, user evidence, and business constraints before acting.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="reference-section split-section" id="ai-output-comparison">
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">AI Output Lab</p>
      <h2>Compare final answers at the observation boundary.</h2>
      <p>The lab accepts a shared prompt and user-pasted visible outputs. It counts words, Markdown headings, list items, explicit URLs, and literal criterion coverage with deterministic browser code.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">What it does not infer</p>
      <h2>No hidden queries. No winner score.</h2>
      <p>The measures do not verify facts, rank models, expose chain of thought, or prove which private tools and searches produced an answer. Provider names are editable labels for the text the user observed.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/lab/">Open the comparison lab <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="reference-section split-section" id="ownership">
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Ownership</p>
      <h2>Common ownership is disclosed.</h2>
      <p>SEO Fan-out is operated by the Contextter research and product function. Contextter is not an independent source or validator of this framework. The tool remains complete without a Contextter account or handoff.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="mono-label">Corrections</p>
      <h2>The framework is versioned.</h2>
      <p>Report unclear rules, incorrect source descriptions, accessibility problems, or reproducibility failures in the public repository.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/lia-xim/seo-fanout.com/issues">Open a correction issue <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>